/*
 * genAppMisc.goc -- GenApplicationClass and UIApplicationClass, after
 * genAppMisc.asm, which has their class records; the methods of
 * GenApplicationClass are in genAppAttDet.goc, genAppCommonIACP.goc and
 * here, each beside its asm file.
 *
 * GenApplicationClass: the top of the usable and
 * enabled checks (GenCheckIfFullyUsable), the class of the specific UI
 * it is built into, its state, and its part in the life of the process
 * (procClass.goc): the startup on its field, the attach (usable, the
 * active list and the windows), the detach, the close and shutdown
 * (off the field), and the quit levels.
 *
 * Port32 (Port32/ABI.md section 13x):
 *  - the application asks no field for its specific UI
 *    (MSG_SPEC_GUP_QUERY's GenReturnParams hold no 32-bit handle); it
 *    takes GAI_specificUI, else the UI's own (UserGetSpecificUI);
 *  - without a field in its AppLaunchBlock it goes on the system's
 *    default field (the asm asked the specific UI's system,
 *    MSG_SPEC_GUP_QUERY_VIS_PARENT);
 *  - MSG_GEN_APPLICATION_IACP_REGISTER has its parameter, the
 *    IACPServerMode (CL in the asm, missing in the C prototype);
 *  - not yet: state files and the restart list of the field, transparent
 *    detach, the floating keyboard, the removable disk list, the
 *    activation dialog, the save options query on quit.
 *
 * UIApplicationClass, the UI's own application object: its geode's
 * parent object is the system object (so that a system modal dialog of
 * the UI gets the system's focus through it), a focus below it is given
 * the application's focus, keys that come up to it are eaten (but F1,
 * the help), and when nothing below it has the focus any more it lets
 * go of its own and the system finds the focus again.  Not yet: the
 * hard icon bar's keyboard (MSG_META_NOTIFY, GWNT_HARD_ICON_BAR_FUNCTION
 * and GWNT_STARTUP_INDEXED_APP: the floating keyboard is not ported),
 * the mouse and ink messages ignored once the specific UI is gone on a
 * shutdown (UIAppPreventCrashOnShutdown).
 */
